Impact
An unauthenticated attacker can:

    Take over any existing account (admin@chobani.com etc.) without credentials, password, or valid Google token.
    Read PII: name, date of birth, gender, mobile number, postal code, state, marketing preferences.
    Write/modify victim profile data including name, location, postal code (demonstrated with persistence).
    Pre-register a victim email (account takeover / doppelganger attack).
    Bypass account lockout - the social flow succeeds even when the target account is accountLocked: true.

Business Impact

    Complete compromise of user accounts and customer trust
    Exposure of personally identifiable information (PII) for all Chobani users
    Regulatory compliance violations (GDPR, CCPA) due to unauthorized access to personal data
    Potential for mass account takeover campaigns
    Reputational damage to Chobani brand

Remediation Recommendations

    Validate the Google/Firebase identity token server-side (signature via JWKS; check iss, aud, exp) before linking an account.
    Never derive emailid/socialUId from unverified client JSON - use confirmed id-token claims only.
    Require proof of email ownership before creating or linking a social login to an existing account.
    Enforce account lockout on all authentication flows, including social login.
    Add rate limiting and anomaly detection on /oauth/sociallogin endpoint.
